ok at my track record  in in dc  and they're going to understand that i'm  the type of leadership  that we need more of in washington i  juxtapose that to dan rhodeimer who is  basically clinging to the  the coattails of this president i  haven't really heard  a plan of what he has for the future  uh basically you know it's one thing to  say you don't like something  but it's another thing to get to work  and try to fix it and i've demonstrated  i have a track record of being able to  do that  donald trump did win cd3 by one point  in 2016. what about that concern and  have voters noticed enough of a change  um to vote democrat  listen um you know donald trump won it  by a point  i i was able to carry this district by  nine points uh  in 2018. um to me  this race is not about donald trump this  race to me  is about the people of southern nevada  i we are ground zero for the economic  devastation  of this pandemic we have a large and  vibrant  community we have a large community of  retirees who are worried about medicare  and social security we have you know  parents who are sending their you know  or teaching their children  online at home and i believe that it  will be a referendum  of not only who is going to help  us rebuild and you know my background  in our community of taking on the  toughest problems  i believe that i'm a member of the  education and labor committee  we have a we have a long path to  get out of this economic crisis but a  lot of it will  obviously go through workforce  development  making sure that we're bringing funds  into our community  to support retraining or training our  workforce  and i've already have a track record of  doing that nevada state college just  announced a two million dollar grant  that i  helped them secure uh to help with their  education  training programs uh especially  important because it's a hispanic  serving institution  and then i also was able to get a  million dollars for  area health education centers again  another  key workforce development program of  making sure we're training people  for jobs of tomorrow and so um  to me i believe that this race is about  someone who's willing to get out there  figure out how we're getting resources  into our state to help us rebuild  uh instead of someone who's going to  repeat  the divisive and violent rhetoric that  we have heard for the past four years  i think people are really tired of the  fear of the violence that we've seen and  they want to see  someone who's actually going to work  together and that's the key difference  uh in this race between myself and dan  rhodeimer  there were several debates on the table  but you did not agree to one  for now why not listen uh  dan rhodeimer had agreed to a pbs debate  um i agreed to it as well and then he  backed out basically  um and so you know it's on to him i  i agreed to a debate he had agreed to we  offered a debate though  huh we also and i had yes and i had said  because of uh basically  his health practices of having rallies  and  events with no mass that i was willing  to do one debate  i accepted the one debate that he had  accepted  and then he turned it down um  we've asked you about this before i'm  going to ask you again  for viewers who may not have seen those  previous interviews  there was controversy about your role  with ppp  loans and your husbands or your family's  business what do you want to say about  that  what happened uh well listen i  i think everyone remembers back in march  when we passed  the cares act the ppp program  one of the key things that was really an  administration  issue that had prevented gaming  companies companies that derived some of  their revenues from gaming  they were prevented from accessing the  key  small business program that was part of  the cares act  simply because they had gaming revenues  i along with  our entire bipartisan delegation not  just here in nevada  across the country many states who have  a large gaming presence  we lobbied to make sure that gaming was  included  in in the ppp program now i want to say  prior to that fix nevada ranked almost  near the bottom  in terms of the percentage of small  businesses that  benefited from the ppp program after  now we have seen close to 45 000  businesses  responsible for half a million jobs have  access to those critical funds i was  doing my job by advocating to make sure  that gaming was included in this program  along with  our entire delegation my husband's  company  i applied for it i had no decision in  their and them applying i had no deci i  had no role  in sba's decision of approving the loan  and i certainly won't have any role in  the repayment  of the loan uh you know they claim that  those funds went to support about 700  jobs  that's exactly what the program was  intended to do to support  employment and it was so important for  our state  uh and it was egregious that gaming was  cut  out of that program and i just did my  job by advocating for that  how concerned are you though that voters  may have heard about this or hear about  this and  think well maybe there is a conflict of  interest and  maybe she's just another politician  who's out for themselves how concerned  are you about that and what would you  say to them  i you know again i'd say that this was  an omission of the key industry  in our state and at a time when to  protect the lives of our fellow nevadans  of americans  we asked major businesses to completely  shut down and gaming was one of them  and it was my duty to make that fight to  make sure that  our main industry our main economy  driver  was covered by this key program um but  ultimately i think people need to look  at my track record  uh 25 years in this community you know i  say look at  what they have done and what the which  will  give you a good idea of what they're  about and what they're going to do  and you know from the minute i got here  i got to work  on key issues facing our most vulnerable  residents whether it was our homeless  community  our school children our kids who are at  risk of dropping out  and so you know i've demonstrated in my  career  that i've been able to get results and  roll up my sleeves and focus on the  issues that affect nevadans  and i think that's what people are going  to be thinking about  especially now as we're looking for who  are we going to have on our side  that's going to look past the political  uh rhetoric and dig in  and get to what we actually need to do  to rebuild our economy  and i think the choice is clear  congresswoman susie lee thank you so  much all right  thanks good talking to you have a good  one you too bye
 

